  "details": "1. Have a radial puppet open in one hand and the scaling radial open in the other\n\n2. move the scaling radial off of whatever value it was set to and lock it in\n\n3. phantom marker appears on the second radial puppet in the same location as the scaling radial.\n\nAdditional Notes:\n\n* This marker does not  have snapping on the new radial like it does on the scaling radial\n\n* disappears when you close and reopen the radial\n\n* Only conditions seem to be that the scaling radial must not be closed on the same value it was opened with and that the other radial needs to be open when the scaling radial is closed. You can move the scaling radial, open the other radial, then close the scaling radial and the phantom marker will still appear.",
